# Intent: Give back the internal RAM the merged image used (memory gate, 2026-11-16: the largest free internal block was 8,704 bytes against a gate of 16,000; the consolidated image had 25,600). Two transient tasks took internal stack while the wake word model loads, and the model then settled around them: the "mm" render task (3 KB) now runs once at the start of the listening ring task, whose stack is in PSRAM, and the pack boot task (6 KB, reads the flash cache) starts from a timer 15 s after boot instead of at registration. The long descriptions of seven new tools (prefs.set, overlay.set, listen.test, pack.status, remote.session, remote.action, remote.say) are shortened: tool descriptions live in internal heap for the life of the unit, 1.9 KB in all. Statics that sat in internal RAM move to PSRAM: the overlay engine state (1.35 KB), the pack directory, receive state and held-pack names (1.2 KB) and the filler u-law table (0.5 KB). Bench builds also log two trace lines (listen_wake_in, listen_cue_queued) so wake to first sound can be timed. No behaviour changes; a stored look pack applies 15 s after boot instead of at once.
# Placement: unit (boot memory)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/{maipai_listen.cc,maipai_packs.cc,maipai_fx.cc,maipai_remote.cc,maipai_filler.cc} (ours, TB01, TB02, TA01, TA03, TB05)
# Check after a flash: the memory line after 20 s shows int_big at least 16,000 and internal_min at least 15,000; self.pack.status says booted true after 20 s; a wake plays the mm cue (listen_sound mm).

